# 22. SERVER-SIDE AUTHORIZATION RULES

Implement authorization for every protected endpoint.

Determine access using the authenticated identity, resource ownership, active document grants, current organisation membership, applicable workspace policy, and any explicit administrative policy.

Enforce the following initial rules:

NONE:
- No document-content access.
- No download.
- No edit.
- No permission management.

READ:
- Read, preview, and download only when policy allows.
- No content edits.
- No permission management.

EDIT:
- READ capabilities.
- Permitted content or metadata changes.
- No automatic permission management.
- No automatic deletion rights.

OWNER:
- Document management and permission management according to policy.

An organisation administrator does not automatically receive document-content access.

An organisation member does not automatically receive access to every company document.

The backend must validate:
- Document read.
- Document preview.
- Document download.
- Document modification.
- Document deletion.
- Permission listing.
- Permission creation.
- Permission modification.
- Permission revocation.
- Workspace access.
- Member management.
- Invitation management.
- Audit access.

Do not implement authorization only in Angular.

Do not accept an effective permission value from the frontend as an authoritative input.

Where possible, implement reusable ASP.NET Core authorization handlers and policies.

Ensure that revoked grants and revoked memberships are reflected in subsequent protected requests.

Prevent cross-tenant access at both the query and authorization layers.

